scription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-22T17:04:28Z","updated_at":"2026-06-01T11:52:55Z","closed_at":"2026-06-01T11:26:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119663","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119663","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119663.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119663.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #118666 \r\n- Closes #119782\r\n\r\n## Summary of changes\r\n\r\nWhen `HTTPRequest.cancel_request()` is called, it sets a flag in `HTTPClient`, which is checked by the thread that is reading from data from the peer in blocking mode, and if it's set, then it returns, breaking an endless loop. This prevents a deadlock when for example the Ethernet cable is unplugged during the request, and then it is cancelled, which would freeze the main thread.\r\n\r\n```\r\nHTTPRequest.cancel_request() -> HTTPClient.cancel_response_read() -> break infinite while loop\r\n```\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119782*","closed_by":{"login":"NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev","html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/